※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4480 LANG_PURE_CALLS_IMPURE

※ A condition is pure whatever the function it belongs to may do.  One whose
※ checking changed something could not be compiled out, and a build that
※ compiled it out would run a different program -- so the purity rules are
※ asked of the clause on its own, and the note says why.

let counter: mut u8 = 0u8

@[impure]
fn step(a: u8) → u8 pre(bump(a) > 0u8):
    a

@[impure]
fn bump(a: u8) → u8:
    counter ← a
    a

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(step(1u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
